From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:13:50 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-combo: Keep the orientation a partner reports
 while the PHY runs USB4

In USB4 mode the orientation switch forgets the orientation on every
call: it has nothing to program then. But the setting is still needed
afterwards. A partner can leave USB4 for USB 3 without being plugged in
again (an NVMe enclosure that is given no PCIe tunnel does), the
alternate mode driver repeats the orientation with that mode change
while the PHY is still in USB4 mode, and the PHY is then reconfigured
for USB 3 with no orientation, which it treats as normal. With the plug
reversed the SuperSpeed lanes are on the other pair, and the device
connects at high speed:

  PAN port 1 orientation 1 version 1 mux 1 ...
  qmp_combo_reconfigure_phy: switching from qmpphy mode 3 to 2
  usb 3-1: new high-speed USB device number 2 using xhci-hcd

(2 of 2 with the plug reversed; SuperSpeed Plus with it normal.)

Keep the orientation in USB4 mode and only leave the hardware alone.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.2
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c | 14 ++++++++------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
index 758d609a2..ba05d9680 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -5581,18 +5581,20 @@ static int qmp_combo_typec_switch_set(struct typec_switch_dev *sw,
 {
 	struct qmp_combo *qmp = typec_switch_get_drvdata(sw);
 
-	if (qmp->qmpphy_mode == QMPPHY_MODE_USB4) {
-		/* QMPPHY has no orientation handling in USB4 mode, don't cache the setting */
-		qmp->orientation = TYPEC_ORIENTATION_NONE;
-		return 0;
-	}
-
 	if (orientation == qmp->orientation || orientation == TYPEC_ORIENTATION_NONE)
 		return 0;
 
 	guard(mutex)(&qmp->phy_mutex);
 	qmp->orientation = orientation;
 
+	/*
+	 * The PHY has no orientation in USB4 mode. Keep the setting for the
+	 * mode that follows: a partner can leave USB4 for USB 3 or DisplayPort
+	 * without being plugged in again, and the orientation is not sent anew.
+	 */
+	if (qmp->qmpphy_mode == QMPPHY_MODE_USB4)
+		return 0;
+
 	if (qmp->init_count)
 		return qmp_combo_reconfigure_phy(qmp, qmp->qmpphy_mode);
 
